  "detail": "This is the last review round. The freshness sentinel, the `--` refusal and the fabricated-`met` refusal are right, and each test fails without its fix.\n\nOne regression, reproduced: the round's prose scan (~233, with the rejection at ~213) treats any occurrence of 'Factory gate' in a row's evidence as a citation, so a sandbox-blocked verifier quoting `bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title'` can't get substitution even with a valid passing factory record for that exact test. Validate only the structured citation fields (`gateEvidence` and the covering-test record reference) against factory records for the same SHA. Remove the prose scanner, the exact prose-citation consumer (~195) and the recursive eligibility reconstruction (~240): the binding doesn't need them, and the issue's budget was about 120 lines against 562 in this PR. Free text in `evidence` is never authority, in either direction.\n\nAdd these regression tests from review (they fail on this PR; adjust helpers, don't weaken them):\n\n```ts\ntest(\"quoted factory-like test titles do not prevent covering-test binding\", () => {\n  const run = coveringRun();\n  run.name = \"Factory gate literal title\";\n  if (!run.result) throw new Error(\"missing result\");\n  run.result.command = \"bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title' './x.test.ts'\";\n  run.result.coveringTest = { file: run.file, name: run.name };\n  const value = {\n    ...requested,\n    criteria: requested.criteria.map((c) => ({\n      ...c,\n      evidence: \"Attempted bun test -t 'Factory gate literal title' x.test.ts: EPERM in sandbox\",\n      covering_tests: [{ file: run.file, name: run.name }],\n    })),\n  };\n  expect(bindCovering(value, [run]).criteria[0]?.status).toBe(\"met\");\n});\n```"
